# Fixtures are deliberately shaped — a formatter rewriting them changes what they test.
test/fixtures

# The same fixtures again, seen through the session worktrees the agent tooling nests inside
# the repository. A pattern containing a slash is anchored to this file's directory, so
# `test/fixtures` above does not match the copy at .claude/worktrees/<session>/test/fixtures —
# and a deliberately malformed fixture found down there turned `npm run check` red for anyone
# holding a session worktree, while CI stayed green on a fresh checkout that has none.
# Git ignores this directory via .git/info/exclude, which prettier does not read.
.claude/worktrees

# And awcli's own runtime directory, which is the same trap one tool over: a run provisions a whole
# checkout of this repository at .awcli/run/worktrees/<run>/<slot>, so `npm run format` would rewrite
# the source files a live agent is working in — foreign uncommitted work, edited by a formatter nobody
# asked. Git ignores it via the generated ignore line (BR-030), which prettier does not read.
.awcli

# Design artifacts are approved documents, not source. A code formatter must never
# rewrite them — a whitespace diff on an approved manifest is noise at best and an
# unreviewed change at worst.
.atelier
